p><b>Albarradas Sign Language</b>, also known as <b>Didxa ná’</b>, is an indigenous village sign language of Mexico. It arose approximately 150 years ago in the Zapotec villages of Santa Catarina Albarradas, San Antonio Albarradas and possibly one other nearby town, due to a high incidence of congenital deafness.</p>"}